 sandwiches and drinking beer  inside there is no suggestion that kia  stammer broke the rules or broke the law  it is ridiculous we weren't allowed to  do that at that time were we  you know everything that he did was in  line with the rules what we know how the  prime minister said well he did well the  prime minister concedes all of this  happened we've just had a various kind  of strange excuses as to exactly what's  going on but you know i think the  british people can see for themselves  what's happening here i think it's now  for senior conservative politicians for  the conservative party to think whether  they really want to continue to put the  country through this it's time the prime  minister just did the decent thing and  resigned they're so mired in scandal and  are making excuses for what's been going  on that they're not in a position to  tackle the cost of living crisis that  families are facing we however have got  a clear plan for how we provide support  for families with those gas and  electricity bills that are so high this  winter with you know support for every  family but extra help for those that  need it most with a windfall tax on oil  and gas providers he was accosted by  somebody with a bit of cake you know you  can't criticize him for that  i mean it's hard to know where to begin  with this litany of utterly utterly  ridiculous excuses they seem to think  the conservative party and all of these  ministers that are wheeled out every day  seem to think that we're all idiots we  can see what's going on the british  people know what has gone on it's time  the prime minister for the first time in  his life just did the decent thing and  went you're not going to not unless he's  forced to well this is why it really is  for the conservative party now to think  whether they're prepared to continue to  prop up this prime minister who we all  know has lied and lied a little bit  i mean i've had ministers on the program  over the last two days three days we saw  dominic rob in the house yesterday in  the uh central lobby lots of them are  all saying they've got um his um for  some support  well they've obviously got law of  self-respect and no respect actually for  the institutions of our country if  that's the way that they go on because  when the british people were doing what  was asked of them when children were  mainly at home when they weren't able to  go to school when nhs staff were working  in intensive care when our bus drivers  were going out to work delivery drivers  when everyone was following the rules  doing what was asked of them in the way  that we always behave in britain the  prime minister number 10  people there were wheeling in suitcases  of boost to have parties i mean it's  just complicated  we don't know yet we don't know we have  to wait for the sugar report don't we  well i don't think instead once or twice  on this show  well i think we all want to see it but  the government shouldn't seek to use sue  grey as a shield to defend what's  frankly indefensible what we can all see  for ourselves and what the british  people know to be the case but if you  ask for an investigation and that's what  you asked for then you have to wait for  the results um if it doesn't come today  probably won't come tomorrow so it could  be pushed into next week what will  labour be doing about that what would  you be saying about that well we want to  see it of course we do but what we what  we are prepared to wait well we want to  see it as soon as possible the british  people want to see it but let's not  pretend that the sue grey report is the  answer to all of the problems that we  face here she's a civil servant doing  her job diligently i'm sure  but you know we know what's going on the  prime minister has admitted what has  gone on it's just this litany of bizarre  excuses what we're focused on as an  opposition is making sure that we've got  the answers to the real challenges  facing the country a